WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.272
Unsupervised learning finds structure in data without being given the correct labels in advance.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:12.544
Sorting a mixed box means grouping objects by similarities, without names supplied in advance.

00:00:12.544 --> 00:00:18.816
The system compares examples using measurable features, then detects recurring relationships.

00:00:18.816 --> 00:00:25.088
A clustering algorithm may form groups, but the groups do not automatically mean “cat” or “dog.”

00:00:25.088 --> 00:00:31.360
Normal activity patterns can help flag unusual examples as possible anomalies.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:37.632
Unsupervised learning finds structure in data without predefined labels; people inspect whether the result is useful.
